# File decomposition

Do not let pages, components, controllers, or services become dumping grounds. Extract **named units of work** into their own files so modules stay readable and swappable when design/logic changes.

## Default posture

- **One primary export per file** when the unit has a clear name (`map-api-error.ts`, `auth-cookies.ts`, `use-my-profile.ts`)
- Host file = wiring/composition; extracted file = the behavior
- Prefer **colocated** extracts next to the feature over a global `utils/` junk drawer

## Extract when (any)

- File is heading past ~150–200 lines **or** has 2+ unrelated concerns
- Logic is reusable (or clearly will be) across components/services
- Pure helpers, mappers, validators, cookie/JWT utils, formatters
- React: non-trivial state/effects → `hooks/use-*.ts`; presentational chunks → sibling components
- Nest: non-trivial branching → private collaborators or `*.helper.ts` / use-case module — keep controllers thin
- Tests get clearer when the unit is imported alone

## Do not extract when

- 5–15 line glue used once next to its only caller (KISS / YAGNI)
- Trivial one-liners that only make navigation worse
- “Future reuse” with a single call site and no clear name

## Placement

| Kind | Where |
|------|--------|
| UI primitive | `apps/web/components/ui/` |
| Feature UI / hook | next to the feature (`components/<feature>/`, `hooks/`) |
| Web lib helper | `apps/web/lib/<name>.ts` |
| API helper | next to domain (`auth/auth-cookies.ts`) — not inside the controller |
| Shared contract | `@nechto/api-contract` / `@nechto/api-client` |

```ts
// ❌ BAD — profile-editor.tsx owns fetch mapping, avatar MIME checks, and form UI
// ✅ GOOD — map-api-error.ts + ProfileAvatar.tsx + profile-editor.tsx composes them
```

## Naming

- File name = what it does (`jwt-expires.ts`, not `helpers2.ts`)
- No catch-all `utils.ts` / `misc.ts` / `helpers.ts` that accumulates unrelated exports
- If a “utils” file grows a second theme — split by theme immediately
